# The book-to-skill tree is byte-pinned to upstream commit c6bc1b79 and every
# path's SHA-256 is recorded in tests/codex_skills/test_upstream_manifest.py.
#
# The pinned blobs are CRLF, and three lines of book_to_skill/utils.py are not —
# so this tree is not safely normalizable in either direction. With this repo's
# core.autocrlf=true and no attribute here, Git stores an LF-normalized copy and
# restores CRLF on checkout; a fresh clone would then disagree with the recorded
# digests, and re-deploying from it would ship bytes that are not the audited
# ones. `-text` freezes the bytes exactly as they were audited.
book-to-skill/** -text
